  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 230 PM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nThe cooler temperatures will last through the end of the week and \nupcoming weekend. Keep in mind, while these temperatures may feel \ncooler compared to last week, they will typical for this time of \nyear. The average high for this time of year is 77 in Mason City, 80 \nin Des Moines, and 81 in Ottumwa. After a couple dry days a \nshortwave embedded in zonal flow will pass across Iowa on Friday and \nbring the next round of convection to the area. A more robust system \nSunday into early next week with bring additional shower and \nthunderstorm chances to the area. These successive systems will\nhelp to knock a few more degrees off high temperatures. At this\ntime range there is uncertainty on the timing and track of \nthese systems, but guidance does agree that cooler temperatures \nfilter in by early to middle of next week.",
